**Summary**
- Bug: lesson toolbar's section-progress-pill counted only `sectionState[id].done`, ignoring the page-level `autoDone` (set by widget `onComplete`) and `manuallyCompletedSections` — so completing a Quiz/Code/DragMatch/etc. didn't update the pill until reload.
- Fix: extracted `countDoneSections(lesson, flags)` in `src/lib/lessons/advance.ts` alongside the existing `isSectionDone` / `areAllSectionsDone`, then routed the lesson page's `sectionTotals` useMemo through it with all three completion sources. Added `aria-label="X of Y completed"`, `role="status"`, `aria-live="polite"` on the pill.
- Tests: 5 new unit tests including the bug reproduction (`liveAutoDone={s1:true} → 1/2`). Typecheck clean, 331/331 vitest pass.
- Browser-verified on `quiz-test/single-select`: pill went 0/4 → 1/4 (+aria) live after answering one Quiz, then 0/4 on navigating to `multi-select` (`/tmp/us079-after-correct.png`, `/tmp/us079-second-lesson.png`).
